Here's an example of how to style a table with alternating background colors for rows using CSS:

``` css
/* Default table styling */
table {
  border-collapse: collapse;
  width: 100%;
}

/* Style for even rows */
table tr:nth-child(even) {
  background-color: #f2f2f2;
}

/* Hover effect for rows */
table tr:hover {
  background-color: #ddd;
}

/* Style for table head */
table th {
  background-color: #222;
  color: #fff;
  padding: 10px;
}

/* Style for table data */
table td {
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
  padding: 8px;
  text-align: left;
}
```

In this CSS code, we use the `nth-child` selector to add background color to every even numbered row. We also add a hover effect on the rows to highlight them when the user hovers over them. In addition, we add specific styles to the table head and data cells. 

Here's an example of how to apply these styles to an HTML table:

``` html
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Item</th>
      <th>Price</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Apple</td>
      <td>$1.00</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Banana</td>
      <td>$0.50</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Orange</td>
      <td>$0.75</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Pear</td>
      <td>$1.25</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
```

By default, every even numbered row will have a light gray background color, and when a user hovers over a row, the background color will change to a darker gray.

