table td {
  border: 1px solid #ddd;
  padding: 8px;
  text-align: center;
  border-radius: 10px;
}

/* Style for table footer */
table tfoot {
  background-color: #444;
  color: #fff;
  border-radius: 10px;
}

/* Style for table footer cells */
table tfoot td {
  border: none;
  padding: 10px;
  text-align: center;
  border-radius: 10px;
}
```

In this updated CSS code, we added a style for `tfoot`, which sets the background color to `#444` and the text color to white using the `color` property. We also added a style for `tfoot td`, which removes the border from the table cells in the footer using the `border` property and sets the `padding` to `10px` to add space around the text.

Now, to add a footer to your HTML table, just add a `tfoot` tag at the end of the `table` tag like this:

``` html
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Item</th>
      <th>Price</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Apple</td>
      <td>$1.00</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Banana</td>
      <td>$0.50</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Orange</td>
      <td>$0.75</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Pear</td>
      <td>$1.25</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
  <tfoot>
    <tr>
      <td colspan="2">Total: $3.50</td>
    </tr>
  </tfoot>
</table>
```

The `tfoot` tag contains a `tr` tag which contains a `td` tag. The `colspan` attribute is used to span the table to two columns to match the columns in the table. This adds a footer row to your table with a background color of `#444` and a border-radius of `10px`.
